WEBVTT

00:00:05.910 --> 00:00:12.578
Grouping organizes a detail list into meaningful sections. Each group can add a heading, subtotal, or both.

00:00:20.587 --> 00:00:26.060
Open the fictional Department Revenue report. Its visits are grouped by department and then doctor.

00:00:30.649 --> 00:00:36.602
A group header appears when its value changes. The outer Department group contains a nested Doctor group.

00:00:41.475 --> 00:00:49.257
Select the Department group to see its grouping field and sort settings. The data is still the source list; the report adds structure around it.

00:00:53.841 --> 00:00:59.074
A Doctor subtotal belongs in its group footer, so it appears after that doctor’s visits.

00:01:03.318 --> 00:01:08.009
The Department footer adds a higher-level subtotal after all doctors in that department.

00:01:12.152 --> 00:01:17.389
The data footer appears once after all groups and records, for the overall report total.

00:01:22.966 --> 00:01:34.005
Preview the PDF and follow the department headers, doctor subtotals and final total from top to bottom. This is a useful pattern for sales, operations, and clinical summaries.
